Sport Scientist at Baylor University working with Football GPS and force plate data.

**Role:** Primary builder and user of athlete performance data pipelines. Also hands off running scripts to assistant coaches and directors during season.

**Technical profile:**
- Comfortable in Python and R
- Windows 11 machine, project folders on OneDrive (can cause DuckDB file locks)
- Python 3.14.x via the Python Install Manager (never WinGet/Chocolatey) — see [[project-python-environment]]
- Go installed at `C:\Program Files\Go\bin`
- Prefers local SQLite/DuckDB over cloud — Baylor IT approval required for cloud solutions

**Working style:**
- Direct — says "stop" or "we can call it done" when finished, no ceremony needed
- Prefers tangible working examples over documentation
- Builds incrementally; has started/stopped projects multiple times due to API friction
- Will share credentials and tokens directly in conversation when needed for testing

**Active projects:**
- [[project-catapult-cli]] — GPS CLI built with Printing Press, now wrapped as the `pp-catapult-openfield-connect` skill

**Design preferences:**
- Nothing that breaks mid-season and requires significant effort to fix
- Transparent, editable pipelines
- No web servers, schedulers, or cloud dependencies without IT approval
